  {
    "index": 3,
    "hash": "70HhyU51ag+uSJF5ft3Wf5ZP8Fs=",
    "timestampUtcMs": "2026-08-13T14:38:58.651Z",
    "action": {
      "type": "SET_CONTENT",
      "input": {
        "content": "This is one of the few places the Powerhouse docs record the reasoning behind an API choice rather than just the choice.\n\nThe team started with the built-in `Date`. The problem is not that `Date` cannot represent UTC \u2014 `new Date('2024-12-25T14:46:22.001Z')` parses UTC fine \u2014 it is that the resulting object is a local-time object with **no way to ask whether it was constructed from a UTC timestamp**. You can call the constructor and end up with a different instant than the one you thought you passed in, and nothing in the type or the object tells you. `toISO()` will happily emit a UTC string either way.\n\nStrings were considered and rejected: they carry their own class of problems and are only checkable at runtime.\n\nluxon's `DateTime` carries time, date, and timezone in one object, and the docs' summary of why it won is characteristically blunt: it is \"difficult (but not impossible) to create a luxon `DateTime` object with a timezone you weren't intending to use.\" For a time-series analytics system, where a silent timezone shift moves numbers into the wrong bucket rather than producing an error, that difficulty is the feature.\n\nThe consequence is that luxon appears on both sides of the API: `AnalyticsSeriesInput.start`/`end` and `AnalyticsQuery.start`/`end` are `DateTime`, and `GroupedPeriodResult.start`/`end` come back as `DateTime`. Series insertion in the shipped processors uses `DateTime.fromISO(operation.timestampUtcMs)`, so the operation log's own UTC timestamp is the input rather than any local clock reading \u2014 which also keeps analytics writes deterministic under replay.\n\nProvenance: draft `03-Build/04-WorkWithData/_06-Analytics Engine/typescript/index.md` (\"A note about times\"); luxon imports confirmed across `packages/analytics-engine/{core,browser,knex}/src/` and `packages/shared/processors/drive-analytics/` at 6.2.2-dev.45.",
        "updatedAt": "2026-08-13T14:38:57.000Z"
      },
      "timestampUtcMs": "2026-08-13T14:38:58.651Z"
    }
  },
